Bots filled into an LFG dungeon group reach the dungeon and the group keeps
1 tank / 1 healer / 3 dps (supersedes the per-add teleport in 0037).

Touches: modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.{h,cpp}
         (FillLfgRaidGroup, new ProcessLfgFillTeleports, RespecBotForRole log)
No tracked src/server/ files change -- no core diff in this record; it documents
gitignored module edits.

Why: report #151 / issue #149 (post-ship 0.1.104) -- "playerbots still not being
summoned on joining a LFD group, nor are we getting 1 tank, 1 healer, 3 dps
(seems to be 1 tank/healer and 4 dps usually)".

Summon gap root cause: 0037's per-add teleport read the destination from the
LEADER's selected dungeons (LFGMgr::GetSelectedDungeons). A random-queue group
(the common case) stores the RANDOM entry there (e.g. 258 Random Classic), and
random entries never get entrance coords: LFGMgr::LoadLFGDungeons fills coords
for every type EXCEPT LFG_TYPE_RANDOM (LFGMgr.cpp ~325) and lfg_dungeon_template
has no rows for 258/259/260 -- so the fill teleported bots to (0, 0, 0) on
map 0. The PROPOSAL dungeon, by contrast, is always a specific dungeon (the
queue expands random selections via GetDungeonsByRandom, LFGQueue.cpp ~481), so
the real player teleported fine and the bots did not.

Fix: the per-add teleport is replaced by a deferred pass. FillLfgRaidGroup
enqueues each added bot; ProcessLfgFillTeleports (called from UpdateAIInternal
every pass) re-reads the group's OWN dungeon id, which MakeNewGroup writes
(LFGMgr.cpp:1862, right after the fill hook returns) and which is the specific
proposal dungeon even for random queues. Guards mirror LFGMgr::TeleportPlayer's
refusals (dead, combat, falling, fatigue, charm, mid-teleport) but RETRY each
pass until a 10s deadline instead of dropping the bot with a client-side error
the bot never sees. A bot MakeNewGroup already teleported (raid fills) is left
alone.

Role gap root cause: the fill's fallback path added any idle bot when no tank/
healer-shaped bot existed in the level band, silently padding groups with dps.
Fix: the fallback now prefers a class that CAN play the wanted role
(ClassCanFillRole) and respeccs it via the existing RespecBotForRole (talents
+ gear, verified against the resulting talent tab) before being added.

Diagnostics: the fill instrumentation previously logged on the "playerbots"
category, which is NOT configured in live worldserver.conf (Logger.root=2) --
no "Filled LFG raid group" / "Respecced bot" line could EVER appear in
Server.log, which is why #151 arrived with zero log evidence. All fill lines
now use "module.playerbots.lfg", which inherits the live Logger.module=4:
  - "LFG fill: added {} bot(s) to a group of {}/{} ({} tank, {} healer, {} dps;
    wanted {}/{} tank/healer)"
  - "LFG fill: teleported bot {} to dungeon {}"
  - "LFG fill: respecced bot {} to '{}' to cover a wanted role"
  - WARN "LFG fill teleport expired: bot {} never reached the dungeon"
